## 2. kdeglobals – actual UI colors

File: `~/.config/kdeglobals`

Important color groups:

| Section | Controls |
| --- | --- |
| `[Colors:View]` | File view background and text |
| `[Colors:Window]` | Main window background and text |
| `[Colors:Button]` | Buttons |
| `[Colors:Selection]` | Selected files and items |
| `[Colors:Tooltip]` | Tooltips |
| `[Colors:Complementary]` | Complementary UI elements |
| `[Colors:Header]` | Headers |
| `[Colors:Link]` | Hyperlinks |

## 3\. Important color keys

For example:

ini

```ini
[Colors:View]
BackgroundNormal=30,30,30
BackgroundAlternate=38,38,38
ForegroundNormal=220,220,220
ForegroundInactive=160,160,160
ForegroundLink=100,170,255
ForegroundVisited=180,140,220

[Colors:Selection]
BackgroundNormal=50,100,160
ForegroundNormal=255,255,255

[Colors:Window]
BackgroundNormal=35,35,35
ForegroundNormal=220,220,220
```

RGB values are decimal numbers from 0–255.

## 4\. Where to edit color schemes

System Settings/Color - KDE UserBase Wiki

KDE color schemes

`~/.local/share/color-schemes/`

Files have the extension `.colors`.

The color scheme is the best place to customize Dolphin's background, text, selection and alternating row colors.

