## 5\. Apply changes

After editing:

bash

```bash
kbuildsycoca6
```

Then restart Dolphin:

bash

```bash
kquitapp6 dolphin
dolphin &
```

## 6\. Example: dark Dolphin with no alternating row colors

ini

```ini
[Colors:View]
BackgroundNormal=30,30,30
BackgroundAlternate=30,30,30
ForegroundNormal=220,220,220
ForegroundInactive=150,150,150
```

This gives the file list a uniform dark background.

Tip: If you want to customize every aspect of Dolphin independently, edit a copy of your `.colors` theme rather than modifying `kdeglobals` directly. This avoids affecting other KDE applications.
